data: {"choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"I've written up three ways to build the app, with a recommendation.\n\n- **A. Light and simple:** The screen is animated with built-in browser effects, and your saved cities stay in your browser. It would take about 3–5 hours to build and cost nothing to run. It runs smoothly on phones, but the look is stylised rather than realistic.\n- **B. Rich, realistic scenes:** It draws thousands of raindrops and snowflakes, and it looks the most impressive. It would take about 10–16 hours and may stutter or drain the battery on older phones.\n- **C. Mix of both, plus a small server:** It keeps your cities on a server and eases the load on the free weather service. It would take about 12–20 hours and cost a few dollars a month. It also means we store some of your data, which goes against the \"no accounts, nothing stored\" idea.\n\nI recommend **A**, with rain and snow made a bit richer. It stays free, works well on phones, and fits what you asked for. You can move to B or C later if you want more.\n\nPlease confirm one thing. With A, saved cities disappear if you clear your browser data, and they don't carry over between devices. Is that acceptable?"},"finish_reason":null}]}

